Menivor's own native (TikTok / YouTube / Instagram) and extended
(Facebook / LinkedIn / X / Threads / Pinterest / Bluesky / Discord / Mastodon /
Telegram) publishing-connector and OAuth modules
(apps/api/app/domains/publishing/**) were already built, independently, before
this review (2026-10-15) and are not a port of Postiz — do not read the
presence of this NOTICE as "Postiz code ships here" wholesale.

One concrete adaptation was made after comparing both codebases:

* `apps/api/app/domains/publishing/connectors/tiktok.py` — the
  `_classify_error` table (TikTok Content Posting API `error.code` → a
  specific, human-readable message + retryable flag) is adapted from the
  error-code classification table in Postiz's
  `libraries/nestjs-libraries/src/integrations/social/tiktok.provider.ts`.
  No literal source lines were copied; the table of TikTok error codes and
  their meaning was reproduced in this module's own idiom (tuple table +
  substring match) to fit Menivor's `PublishError(message, retryable)`
  contract.

